.th CTIME III 10/15/73
.sh NAME
ctime, ijtime  \*-  convert date and time to ASCII
.sh SYNOPSIS
.ft B
char *ctime(tvec)
.br
long tvec;
.s3
char *ijtime()
.br
.ft R
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Ctime
converts a time in the long int
.it tvec
such as returned by time (II)
into ASCII
and returns a pointer to a
character string
in the form
.s3
    Sun Sep 16 01:03:52 1977\\n\\0
.s3
All the fields have constant width.
.s3
.it Ijtime
returns a character string similar to the above, giving the present
system time.
.it Ijtime
is written in assembler.
It is small and very fast.
.sh "SEE ALSO"
time(II)
.sh AUTHOR
Ian Johnstone
(University of New South Wales)
.sh BUGS
